---
.title = "Performance",
.description = "What glowcap costs, as dated measurements you can repeat: wire-path allocation and footprint budgets the build pins, plus benchmark charts.",
.date = .date("2026-06-12T00:00:00"),
.layout = "performance.shtml",
.draft = false,
---

The build pins the costs it can measure deterministically: allocations, copies,
and core state size. The charts are a dated run from one machine, named in the
stamp under the index.

| Question | Section |
| --- | --- |
| Which codec is cheaper for a small call? | [Codec throughput]($link.ref('codec-throughput')) |
| What does one core connection cost? | [Per-connection footprint]($link.ref('per-connection-footprint')) |
| How many allocations does dispatch make? | [Frame ownership and dispatch]($link.ref('frame-ownership-and-dispatch')) |
| What does encrypted iroh add on loopback? | [Encrypted transport round-trip]($link.ref('encrypted-transport-round-trip')) |
| How do glowcap and Goblins compare under one Racket app? | [The same app on glowcap and Goblins]($link.ref('the-same-app-on-glowcap-and-goblins')) |
| What does each client-language stack cost? | [Cost through each language binding]($link.ref('cost-through-each-language-binding')) |
| How does snapshot cost scale? | [Snapshot and restore]($link.ref('time-travel-snapshot-and-restore')) |
| What does a persistent actor cost? | [Persistent actors in Loam]($link.ref('persistent-actors-in-loam')) |

`zig build check` fails if the allocation and size budgets drift.
`zig build perf-check` is a coarse ReleaseFast timing tripwire. The
[steps toward 1.0](https://github.com/jimisaacs/glowcap/blob/main/docs/ladder.md)
list the exact limits.

```=html
<!-- bench:stamp GENERATED by `zig build bench-site-report`; edits are overwritten -->
<p class="bench-stamp"><em>Measured 2026-10-12 on one machine: Linux aarch64, 20 logical CPUs, 122 GiB RAM, Racket v9.3 CS, Spritely Goblins v0.18.0-52-gdcc2b2c5, with the <code>glowcap</code> archives built by Zig 0.17.0-dev.2294+71403f299 in ReleaseFast. The regeneration command is at the bottom of the page.</em></p>
```

All charts use ReleaseFast. Core footprint excludes socket memory. The
half-million column below is core-memory arithmetic, not RSS. A live loopback
run of 500,000 signed sessions is on the 1.0 page linked above.

# [Codec throughput]($section.id('codec-throughput'))

`bench-codec` encodes and decodes the same small method call with
[Syrup](https://github.com/ocapn/syrup) and Cap'n Proto. Compare nanoseconds
per message. MB/s also reflects that Cap'n Proto emits a larger frame. This
benchmark does not measure Cap'n Proto's constant-time access to fields in large
payloads. [Codecs]($link.page('codecs')) covers the choice.

```=html
<!-- bench:codec GENERATED by `zig build bench-site-report`; edits are overwritten -->
<div class="bench-legend"><span><i style="background:var(--teal, #257f88)"></i>Syrup</span><span><i style="background:var(--accent, #c76f18)"></i>Cap'n Proto</span></div><div class="bench-charts">
