<tr><td>2,048</td><td>1.6</td><td>3.9 / 4.1</td><td>2.7 / 3.6</td><td>2.1</td><td>1</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p class="bench-note">Each conversation is one callable actor and four 4,096-byte messages in LMDB with synchronous commits. An asleep call loads the actor's record first. An edit is one call and one durable commit. A restart opens the database in a new Host and answers one call, reading only the record it calls. At 2,048 conversations the Zig heap holds 0.6 KiB per conversation, against 16.8 KiB of records on disk. The heap excludes LMDB's mapped pages, which the operating system caches separately.</p>
